From: thecorporatetractor <marco@azarguard.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:48:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] build: licence-clean profile (Kusto.Language from
 source, no Azure connectors)

Two opt-in MSBuild properties for builds that redistribute lokql:

- KustoLanguageProject=<path to Kusto.Language.csproj> makes KustoLoco.Core
  reference Kusto.Language built from github.com/microsoft/Kusto-Query-Language
  (Apache-2.0) instead of the Microsoft.Azure.Kusto.Language NuGet package,
  which ships under the Azure Data Explorer SDK licence terms.
- LokqlAzureConnectors=false leaves out the commands that query Azure
  (.adx, .loganalytics, .appinsights, .arg, .defender), AppInsightsSupport and
  with it Microsoft.Azure.Kusto.Data and Kusto.Cloud.Platform(.Msal), which
  ship under the same terms.

Defaults are unchanged. LoadGeoCommand and LoadUserAgentCommand used an
extension method from Kusto.Cloud.Platform.Utils for a case-insensitive
comparison; they use string.Equals now.
